mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# NURISH SMART Backend API\n\nBackend canister for the NURISH SMART assessment platform (SD/MI and SMP/MTs). It stores mentor accounts, assessments, questions, student attempts, answers, grading, and mentor notes, and exposes them to the dashboard and student pages.\n\n## Authentication and authorization\n\n- The canister uses Internet Identity. The app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n- A shared application password gates the whole app. Call `unlockApp(password)` once as a signed-in caller to open the gate for that caller's principal; `isAppUnlocked()` reports whether the caller has already unlocked. The password is compared only on the server and is never returned by any query.\n- Role-based access control is provided by the authorization component. The first caller to initialize access control becomes the admin; subsequent callers are regular users. Admin-only endpoints: `listMentors`, `createMentor`, `setMentorActive`, `deleteMentor`.\n- Mentor endpoints require a signed-in (non-anonymous) caller. `mentorLogin(email, password)` binds the caller's principal to a mentor account; `getCallerMentor()` returns that binding. Mentors may only read and change their own assessments and attempts; admins may act on all.\n- Student endpoints (`getAssessmentByToken`, `startAttempt`, `saveAnswer`, `submitAttempt`, `getAttemptResult`) are callable without an account. They are scoped by the assessment share token and the student's participant identifier.\n- A caller that never signed in through the app's own frontend is unregistered even if it belongs to the app's owner, and a signed-in caller derived against a different origin is a different principal than the one the frontend registered.\n\n## Units and encodings\n\n- Timestamps (`createdAt`, `startedAt`, `submittedAt`) are signed nanosecond `Int` values from `Time.now()`.\n- Identifiers (`id`, `assessmentId`, `questionId`, `attemptId`) are `Nat` counters.\n- `educationLevel` is a variant: `#sdMi` or `#smpMts`.\n- `status` on an assessment is `#draft`, `#published`, or `#closed`; on an attempt it is `#inProgress`, `#awaitingReview`, or `#graded`.\n- `kind` on a question is `#multipleChoice`, `#trueFalse`, `#shortAnswer`, or `#essay`.\n- Optional fields (`optionA`..`optionD`, `submittedAt`, `awardedScore`, `mentorComment`, `mentorNote`) are `?T`; `null` means absent.\n- `shareToken` is an opaque text token used to open an assessment for students.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\n- An assessment starts `#draft`, becomes `#published` via `publishAssessment` (which returns its share token), and can be `#closed` via `closeAssessment`.\n- An attempt starts `#inProgress`, moves to `#awaitingReview` on `submitAttempt` (objective questions are auto-graded), and to `#graded` on `finalizeAttempt` once every manual answer is graded.\n- `getAttemptResult` returns a summary only when the attempt is `#graded`; otherwise it returns `null`. Poll it after grading to know when the final result is available.\n- There is no time limit on an attempt.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n- `unlockApp`, `mentorLogin`, `saveAnswer`, `gradeAnswer`, and `finalizeAttempt` are idempotent for the same inputs: repeating them leaves the same stored state.\n- `createAssessment`, `createMentor`, and `startAttempt` allocate a new identifier on each successful call. `startAttempt` resumes an existing in-progress attempt for the same participant instead of creating a duplicate.\n- `submitAttempt` is a no-op returning `null` when the attempt is not `#inProgress`, so a retry after a successful submit does not re-submit.\n- `deleteAssessment` removes the assessment and all of its questions; it returns `false` when the assessment does not exist.\n\n## Errors, traps, and gotchas\n\n- Authorization failures trap with a message such as `Unauthorized: Only admins can manage mentor accounts` or `Unauthorized: You can only change your own assessments`.\n- `mentorLogin` traps with `Invalid email or password` on bad credentials and `This mentor account is inactive` for a deactivated account.\n- `uploadQuestions` validates every row first and traps with `Validasi soal gagal: ...` listing the failing question numbers and reasons; nothing is stored when any row is invalid.\n- `getAssessmentByToken` never returns the answer key; student-facing questions omit `answerKey`.\n- `startAttempt` returns `null` when the assessment is not `#published` or the participant has used all allowed attempts.\n- `gradeAnswer` returns `null` when the caller cannot manage the assessment, the attempt is still `#inProgress`, the question is objective, or the awarded score exceeds the question weight.\n- `finalizeAttempt` returns `null` until every manual answer has been graded."
  };
};
